xactly an additive subgroup; the two bases in H004 have identical included vectors, and stability under every divided power is equivalent to stability under the generated integer algebra. M remains arbitrary. In Proof.lean:14–31, Lift has only a restriction map and its pointwise agreement, and Actions adds restrictions of the three generators and divided powers, not an irreducibility premise. These restrictions are constructed at 1035–1046; agreement and injectivity of M→V make their maps unique. Thus existential Actions does not weaken the conclusion. VK=K⊗ℤM has the same K-vector space and induced action as M⊗ℤK under the canonical flip; this is a semantic identification, not an unimplemented conversion used between two Lean models. Actual localization/residue conversions and intertwining are provided at 440–461,1078–1136,1196–1245. Nontrivial and the universally quantified K-submodule bottom/top alternative supply both target clauses for the actual induced x,y,h. There is no algebraic-closure, positive-l, p>2 or distinct-reduced-weight premise: l=0 and p=2 remain included. The abstract rank-three Chevalley algebra acts through these generators, so invariance under its span is exactly the displayed three invariances, even for a nonfaithful action.\",\"locations\":[\"/endpoints/P/source\",\"/endpoints/P/actual\",\"/endpoints/P/correspondence\",\"/scope/full_target\",\"/scope/parameters\",\"/scope/hypotheses\",\"/documents\"]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"record_review_item","description":"Save an actual own-stage judgment and coverage; does not finish review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"pointer":{"type":"string"},"coverage":{"type":"string","enum":["unread","read","assessed"]},"judgment":{"type":["object","null"],"additionalProperties":true}},"required":["pointer","coverage","judgment"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_review_progress","description":"Read actual own-stage saved judgments and remaining work.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{},"required":[],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_review_blocker","description":"Finish an explicitly incomplete review after a located real defect. Does not grant acceptance.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"finding":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["finding"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"170cbcb9-578f-40fd-adb3-6bfa30e01bfb","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71460,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":923,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":464},"total_tokens":72383,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_041f7af27a83c08f016ae222d7f3c08191a83a1f8fea57faea":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_041f7af27a83c08f016ae222dd0fb88191a2d58686c627b8fa":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_tokens":0,"